  "description": "Long Travel Enduro Frame\nThe Deviate Claymore builds on its award-winning platform with the same uncompromising focus on speed, control, and durability.This full-carbon, high-pivot enduro frame delivers 165 mm of rear travel with exceptional composure at speed, while remaining efficient enough for full days in the saddle.\nEach frame is supplied with the latest Fox Float X2 Factory (2026) rear shock, carefully matched to the Claymore’s suspension characteristics for precise, consistent control throughout the travel.\nThe Claymore is available in both 29” and MX (mullet) configurations.Choose full 29” for maximum rollover speed and stability, or MX for a more agile, playful rear end without sacrificing high-speed confidence.\nCompatible with 170 mm or 180 mm forks, the Claymore can be tuned to suit everything from race stages to big mountain days.\nVoted Pinkbike's \"Enduro Race Bike of Choice\"Winner of Singletrack's \"Editor's Choice Awards\"\n\nMedium Frame Only: Some fork damper adjusters may foul on the bottom of the downtube due to stack height, which varies brand to brand. To solve this if you are using a Cane Creek headset, you can purchase a crown race spacer here.",
